[00:45.37] The snakes and arrows a child is heir to
[00:49.85] Are enough to leave a thousand cuts
[00:59.78] We build our defenses, a place of safety
[01:04.24] And leave the darker places unexplored
[01:19.52] Sometimes the fortress is too strong
[01:24.02] Or the love is too weak
[01:28.58] What should have been our armor
[01:32.17] Becomes a sharp and angry sword
[01:47.54] Our better natures seek elevation
[01:52.96] A refuge for the coming night
[01:57.45] No one gets to their heaven without a fight
[02:10.04] We hold beliefs as a consolation
[02:14.50] A way to take us out of ourselves
[02:20.86] Meditation or medication
[02:25.31] A comfort, or a promised reward
[02:36.18] Sometimes the spirit is too strong
[02:39.73] Or the flesh is too weak
[02:45.18] Sometimes the need is just too great
[02:49.61] For the solace we seek
[02:55.04] The suit of shining armor
[02:58.22] Becomes a keen and bloody sword
[03:04.51] No one gets to their heaven without a fight
[03:13.56] A refuge for the coming night
[03:18.16] A future of eternal light
[03:22.65] No one gets to their heaven without a fight
[04:00.41] Confused alarms of struggle and flight
[04:04.97] Blood is drained of color
[04:10.32] By the flashes of artillery light
[04:14.89] No one gets to their heaven without a fight
